---
aliases:
  - Green Sea
  - Emerald Deep
date: 2026-06-05T16:40:21-04:00
---

An ocean of trees, a thousand miles wide, sits between Calaria and the Tenchwin Sea. Trees a mile tall choke the sunslight from the sky, and many a strange creature prowls its darkened depths. The Green Sea violently resists outside subjugation, and the modern man has all but given up on delving into its deepest regions.

The forest is known by several names. The [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] officially calls it the Verdant Expanse; others say the Green Sea or the Emerald Deep.

At its edge near [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]] the trees are only about a hundred feet tall, and there are no saplings. The forest begins with full-grown trees and only gets larger. Just inside the treeline it is dangerous enough, and the deeper one goes the darker it becomes, until the darkness is magical. Few go past what the locals call the mid-boughs, the deeper reaches where the canopy closes over. Pilgrims enter for a week at a time to be closer to nature and come back.

The great logging concerns of Calaria pulled out: too many workers died, and it grew too expensive. An orc work force that once cut wood here went too deep and met things it could not fight, and left. Old routes into the forest remain, though none wide enough for a car. Strange life fills the wood, among it [[Bestiary/Vermin|deadly mantises]], [[Bestiary/Beasts|glide apes]], [[Bestiary/Beasts|vine snakes]], and [[Bestiary/Beasts|chorister birds]].


Further in, the forest floor turns soft and muddy, though little rain reaches it. Moss and lichen grow on the trunks only above about three feet, and the ground is swept clean of tracks. A wave of muddy water as tall as a person races through the trees, joyful laughter coming from it, humanoid figures forming in the foam for half a second at a time. A whale call sounds once from far off. White lights float about five feet above the ground, each on a gossamer thread that rises past sight into the canopy; those who come near them feel an urge to grab one. Deeper still the canopy shuts out all light and it is permanently dark.

[[Bestiary/Fey|A court of fey]] holds a glade in that darkness, and beyond them their Lady, whose door is marked with a crescent moon.
